.TH NODERUNNER 1 "October 2026" "NodeRunner 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noderunner \- local network scanner and room mapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noderunner
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve a browser interface and scan an authorized IPv4 network using Nmap.
Starting the program performs a real scan. Installing the RPM does not start it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line options without starting a scan.
.TP
.BI --bind " address"
IPv4 listen address. Direct launch defaults to 0.0.0.0;
the packaged system service selects 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI --port " number"
HTTP port (default 8000).
.TP
.BI --target " CIDR"
IPv4 network or single address to scan. Otherwise use the saved target,
or infer a /24 from the local address.
.TP
.B --no-ports
Discover hosts without scanning TCP ports.
.TP
.BI --top-ports " number"
Number of common TCP ports to check (default 30).
.TP
.BI --data-dir " path"
Directory for private registry, token and backups.
.TP
.BI --assets-dir " path"
Directory containing NodeRunner.html and static assets.
.TP
.BI --html " path"
Override the HTML entry point without changing static asset paths.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/noderunner
Read-only application files.
.TP
.I /var/lib/noderunner
Private state selected by the system launcher.
.TP
.I /etc/noderunner/noderunner.conf
Systemd service environment, including NODERUNNER_BIND and NODERUNNER_PORT.
.SH NOTES
The experimental service runs as a non-root user with CAP_NET_RAW, enabling
ARP discovery and raw scans on the directly connected network. Routed or NAT
networks and client isolation can prevent MAC discovery. A plain launch without
raw-network privileges falls back to TCP connect scans. No global file
capabilities or firewall rules are installed. Keep the API token private.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
